    "title": "Boston Marathon Bingo: The predictable things you see along the route",
    "text": "Just as many runners can boast they’ve run the Boston Marathon for years and years, so, too, can many a hearty spectator who lines the streets of Hopkinton, Ashland, Framingham, Natick, Wellesley, Newton, Brookline and Boston every Patriots’ Day.Those who go know there are some sights you can bet the farm you’ll see at one point or another during the morning, afternoon (but hopefully not night) on Marathon Monday. MassLive photojournalist Sebastian Restrepo made photos at the finish line in Boston two years ago but has otherwise never been a spectator during the Boston Marathon, so we sent him to Framingham and Newton to see how people from all walks of life cheer on the more than 30,000 runners.To make it more interesting, we gave him a Marathon Bingo card to see how many things he could find. Some of the Bingo card spots were:Runner dressed as a super heroTear-jerking teams of humanityA celebrityInflatable costumeGiant head on a stickCow bellKiss me signDroneHow many things did Sebastian find? Check out the video above. What items would be on YOUR Marathon Bingo card?And check out how MassLive reporter Chris McLaughlin fared over in Wellesley at the scream tunnel.More Boston Marathon newsNASA legend and Mass. native Sunita Williams completes Boston MarathonHoots, hollers and ‘last hurrahs’ fill the air at Wellesley College ‘Scream Tunnel’Bill and Hillary Clinton greet daughter Chelsea at finish line of Boston Marathon Zdeno Chara completes another Boston Marathon in under 4 hoursJess McClain sets American record for Boston Marathon course",
